{"name":"Refined Chianti","hex":"#8c1b3c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"refined","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of refine"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Precise, freed from imprecision, particularly:\n Sagacious, sometimes  oversubtle or feigning sagacity.\n Subtle, scrupulous, carefully thought out.","Sagacious, sometimes  oversubtle or feigning sagacity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refined"},{"term":"chianti","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Chianti."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chianti"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chianti","blocks":[{"text":"Chianti is an Italian red wine produced in the Chianti region of central Tuscany, principally from the Sangiovese grape. It was historically associated with a squat bottle enclosed in a straw basket, called a fiasco. However, the fiasco is now only used by a few makers of the wine; most Chianti is bottled in more standard-shaped wine bottles. In the late 19th century, Baron Bettino Ricasoli helped establish Sangiovese as the blend's dominant grape variety, creating the blueprint for today's Chianti wines."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Fiasco_di_vino_rosso_da_tavola_Monteriggioni.jpg/330px-Fiasco_di_vino_rosso_da_tavola_Monteriggioni.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chianti","wikidata":"Q750979"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Grand_Duke_CosimoIII_of_Tuscany_by_van_Douven.jpg/250px-Grand_Duke_CosimoIII_of_Tuscany_by_van_Douven.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/88/Grand_Duke_CosimoIII_of_Tuscany_by_van_Douven.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://th